{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1087182-enchanted-the-ritual-of-parted-mists-suggestion","id":1087182,"title":"Enchanted \"The Ritual of Parted Mists\" Suggestion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-03T08:43:17-07:00","id":1087182,"title":"Enchanted \"The Ritual of Parted Mists\" Suggestion","content":"Ritual doesn't break forever after Enchanted mortal becomes Undone (but it still can hurt a lot, depending on the circumstances). And mortal can be enchanted and reawakened again.<br /> <br /> However, there's a catch. When the Ritual is cast, a mortal has to make a very special promise. Geas, if you will. As long, as mortal are true to their word, Enchantment lasts indefinitely. Admittedly, it may be a great deal harder to re-awaken a working, busy adult years after their Undoing, but as long as they remain being true to their word - it remains a possibility.<br /> <br /> If or when mortal breaks their promise, even Enchanted - ritual ends abruptly and painfully, as per rules in C20. Add irony, salt and ash to your taste.\u200b <hr /><br /> Though, if it was me, I'd made it way more personal and whimsical (and not in a <i>good</i> way). Think H.G. Wells <i>&quot;</i><b>The Door in the Wall</b><i>&quot;. </i><br /> <br /> Or let's say, two boys make a vow to &quot;never befriend a girl&quot; or something equally stupid and unrealistic. Losing a friend to Banality might be sad and scary, but the alternative might turn even more bizarre and cruel. <br /> <br /> And may <i>The Golden Rule</i> be with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-05-2017, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T17:23:08-07:00","id":1088010,"title":"","content":"I like that better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T18:04:02-07:00","id":1090068,"title":"","content":"What Zenten said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T07:45:13-07:00","id":1091944,"title":"","content":"this seems a good place to ask this but how many bestowments does an enchanted actually get? im pretty unclear on this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"than